<p>I'm curious how people on HN are using AI day to day, and came up with a list of questions I thought could be interesting to know. No need to answer every question of course, just wanted to get a gut feel how people are using AI.<p>1) What AI subscriptions are you personally paying for? (Claude, ChatGPT/Codex, Cursor, etc)<p>- Which tiers?<p>- Have you purchased multiple subscriptions from the same provider (eg two Claude accounts)?<p>2) Are you using models outside (or instead) of those subscriptions? For example, pay-as-you-go APIs, OpenRouter, or locally hosted models.<p>- Which models and providers?<p>3) What coding harnesses and interfaces are you using? Are you sticking with the default CLIs or IDE integrations, or using alternatives like OpenCode, Pi, Aider, Muse Code, or custom-built harnesses?<p>- What made you switch harnesses (if you switched)?<p>4) Are you using any agent orchestration or swarm tools?<p>- For example, Munder Difflin, Gas Town, Ruflo, or something custom.<p>5) Are you using broader agent platforms like OpenClaw / Hermes Agent / Grok bot / Dots / Muse?<p>- If you are using them, what are your main use cases?<p>-----<p>I know my workflow has differed significantly from a year ago, and so it would be interesting to capture a snapshot today of what people are using and why.</p>
<hr>
